#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""colson-arch-theme — Omarchy-grade theming for GNOME on Arch (and any GNOME distro).

One command themes the whole desktop, live: wallpaper, GNOME Shell (generated), GTK apps
(shipped or generated libadwaita colors, adw-gtk3 by mode), accent + light/dark, icons with
accent-colored folders, cursor, Ghostty / Alacritty / Kitty / foot, tmux, Neovim,
btop, the browser frame, the editor theme — and every open terminal and Neovim recolors
instantly. 133 Omarchy theme bundles (official + community), a live-preview picker,
wallpaper rotation, day/night scheduling, and a true-black monochrome base (Graphite).

Design laws:
  * Nothing from a theme is ever executed — colors are whitelist-extracted from data files.
  * Graphite (true-black monochrome) is the base; every palette is opt-in.
  * Every hook is idempotent and reversible (`theme install` / `theme uninstall`).
  * Zero dependencies beyond Python 3.11+, git, and GNOME. fzf/Ghostty/nvim/btop optional.

by Colson (@colson0x1) · https://github.com/colson0x1/colson-arch-theme · MIT
"""
from __future__ import annotations

